    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "On turn 1 with only Hallowed Fountain and Floodfarm Verge in hand, playing Hallowed Fountain first is suboptimal. Floodfarm Verge can only produce {U} (not {W}) if you don't control a Plains or Island. By playing Floodfarm Verge first on turn 1 (getting {U} from its unconditional tap ability — wait, actually Floodfarm Verge's {U} requires controlling a Plains or Island). So playing Hallowed Fountain first (as a Plains Island) enables Floodfarm Verge to tap for either {W} or {U} on turn 2. However, the question is whether to pay 2 life to have Hallowed Fountain enter untapped on turn 1. Since MiMo has no 1-mana spell in hand, paying 2 life for an untapped Hallowed Fountain on turn 1 would be a waste. If they played it tapped, that's fine sequencing. Looking at the action log, it says 'puts Hallowed Fountain onto the Battlefield' — we don't see whether they paid life. The choice between the two lands on turn 1 is actually correct: Hallowed Fountain should come first to enable Floodfarm Verge. This appears to be the right play.",
