    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Stormchaser's Talent is generally the stronger turn 1 play in this spot. It creates a 1/1 prowess Otter token immediately, and the Class leveling up later provides card advantage (returning an instant/sorcery from graveyard) and eventually token generation. Tiger-Seal is a 3/3 vigilance but taps itself every upkeep and only untaps when you draw your second card each turn, making it unreliable as an early attacker. Additionally, the opponent has Spell Snare mana available (Hallowed Fountain is tapped, so not right now, but in future turns), and Stormchaser's Talent at MV 1 dodges Spell Snare while Tiger-Seal at MV 1 also dodges it - so that's neutral. However, Stormchaser's Talent synergizes much better with the rest of the hand (Boomerang Basics is an instant/sorcery for prowess triggers, and the Talent can later recur it). The Otter token with prowess can grow with spell casts, providing both pressure and flexibility. Tiger-Seal will likely just sit tapped most turns without reliable second-card-draw enablers early.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Tiger-Seal on turn 1",
