      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Stormchaser's Talent on Turn 3 main phase taps out all mana (the card costs {U}, but looking at the board with 4 lands including two Steam Vents and an Island, they have access to 4 mana). Actually, Stormchaser's Talent costs just {U}, so casting it leaves 3 mana open. Wait - re-reading: they have Steam Vents (untapped), Tiger-Seal (tapped), Island, Steam Vents = 3 untapped lands producing up to 3 mana. Stormchaser's Talent costs {U}, leaving 2 mana open. They could hold up Spell Snare ({U}) with the remaining mana. Actually this sequencing is fine - they cast the 1-mana enchantment and still have mana for Spell Snare. However, the opponent has only 2 lands (Hallowed Fountain + Floodfarm Verge), so the opponent is likely casting 2-mana spells. But wait - they should consider playing the Island from hand first before casting spells to have maximum mana available. They have an Island in hand and it's their main phase.",
